// Regression fixture pinning a documented Minor finding from the
// memory-audit-4e final whole-branch review (probe P9), not a bug this
// fix wave changes: `clarusc/cprint.cla`'s `fpWhileStmt` frees a
// text-producing while-condition's per-iteration temp AFTER the
// `if (!(cond)) break;` check, so the FINAL (false) evaluation's temp is
// never reached by any per-iteration free -- it leaks once per loop
// EXECUTION (not per iteration). Bounded, leak-only, same class as the
// while-condition-temp gaps the ARC milestone is expected to close (the
// `fpIfStmt` flag-materialization trick already used elsewhere would fix
// it). Landed here purely to pin the current behavior as a corpus
// regression fixture -- the final-review fix wave (Criticals 1/2) doesn't
// touch `fpWhileStmt`. Expected strict-mode leak count: 2 (see
// ../p9_while_cond.leaks) -- one text object (struct box + data handle)
// from the last `t + "b"` comparison's temp, evaluated once more (and
// found false) after the loop body stops running.

func runP9WhileCond() {
    var p9T: text = "a"
    var p9N: int = 0
    while p9T + "b" == "ab" {
        p9N = p9N + 1
        if p9N > 0 { p9T.append("x") }
    }
    alert("p9 done")
}
